              "text": "**wakehealth.edu** is the official website for **Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist** (formerly known as Wake Forest Baptist Health), a nationally recognized, fully integrated academic medical center and health system based in Winston-Salem, North Carolina. \n\nThe system serves as the academic core of Atrium Health (which is part of the larger Advocate Health enterprise), combining clinical care, medical education, and groundbreaking research.\n\nThe website serves as a primary hub for patients, students, researchers, and healthcare professionals.\n\n---\n\n### Key Services and Features on the Website\n\n#### 1. Patient Care and Resources\n* **Find a Doctor & Location:** Users can search for primary care providers and specialists. The health system operates several hospitals, emergency rooms, urgent care centers, and more than 300 community clinics across northwest North Carolina and southwest Virginia.\n* **MyAtriumHealth Portal:** This is the secure patient portal (powered by Epic MyChart) where patients can schedule appointments, view lab results, message their healthcare providers, refill prescriptions, and pay bills.\n* **Specialized Care Centers:** The website provides information on their nationally ranked specialty services, including:\n  * **Brenner Children\u2019s Hospital** (pediatric care)\n  * **Comprehensive Cancer Center**\n  * **Heart & Vascular Center**\n  * **Neurosciences & Stroke Care**\n  * **Level I Trauma Center** (the region's only Level I pediatric and adult trauma center)\n\n#### 2. Education (Wake Forest University School of Medicine)\nFor students and faculty, the site provides a gateway to **Wake Forest University School of Medicine**, which offers programs in:\n* Doctor of Medicine (MD)\n* Physician Assistant (PA) studies\n* Nurse Anesthesia (CRNA)\n* Graduate programs in biomedical sciences and health equities\n\n#### 3. Research & Clinical Trials\nAs an academic learning health system, the website hosts portals for researchers and details on ongoing clinical trials. Patients can use the site to search for open clinical trials in areas like oncology, aging, and cardiovascular health.\n\n### System Background\nInitially established in Winston-Salem, the system entered into a strategic combination with Charlotte-based **Atrium Health** in 2020. Under this partnership, the Wake Forest University School of Medicine serves as the academic engine of the entire multi-state Atrium Health network, which also includes a second medical school campus in Charlotte.",
